Thanks for the fix @tnytown! I pushed a few changes during review:

- I retargeted the PR to 3.x. 2.x only receives security fixes, and this is a bug fix (an ID with a backslash, like `App\Enum\user`, produced a wrong key or a JS syntax error).
- I added `JSON_INVALID_UTF8_SUBSTITUTE`. With only `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR`, an ID that is not valid UTF-8 made `cache:warmup` fail with a `JsonException`. Before this PR the file was dumped and the browser decoded those bytes as U+FFFD, so the flag keeps that result.
- I added `JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE | JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES`. Keys with non-ASCII characters or `/` keep the same spelling as before in `index.js` and `index.d.ts`. Quotes, backslashes, control characters and U+2028/U+2029 are still escaped.
- Tests: each case now also checks that the expected literal decodes back to the original ID. New cases cover line terminators, slashes and invalid UTF-8. Test methods have `: void`, as on 3.x.
- Everything is squashed into your commit.
